WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.581
So here we have a sample of vanadium. So vanadium
is used to do catalysis, it is used for a

00:00:06.581 --> 00:00:08.109
whole range of different things.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:16.309
So vanadium is the third of the transition
metals and, because it has more electrons,

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:18.320
it has really quite interesting chemistry.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.910
It is also used in nature and there are a
number of mushrooms that are vanadium rich.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:28.869
The amavadins especially is one of the materials.
So here if we open, we can see on our reel

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:34.191
is a very nice sample of vanadium wire. So
this is the elemental vanadium and as you

00:00:34.191 --> 00:00:39.530
can see it is about 0.1 mm in diameter and
there is 20 metres of it on this reel.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:46.170
Some of its compounds are very reactive. I
can remember that my lab mate Paul was working

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:53.239
with a compound called vanadium hexacarbonyl.
He got a sample it was quite expensive, and

00:00:53.239 --> 00:01:00.469
he poured it, it came in a sealed glass vessel
so he cut open the glass and poured it out

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:03.829
and before his eyes it burst into flames and
disappeared.

